tags: cpu, vcpu, cores

The CPU time of one instance, in thousandths of one core.

The value is an integer. Example: 1500 is one and a half cores. In each period of
100 milliseconds, the processes of the instance use at most value/1000 times
100 milliseconds of CPU time, summed over all their virtual CPUs. The guest has
ceil(value/1000) virtual CPUs, and at least one.

An absent value says nothing (it is not 0). Valid in the resources of a container. The
node reserves the value, keeps the sum of its instances within its capacity, enforces
it, and charges for it.

